  ('[SCENARIO] Your AI-powered loan approval system approves 70% of male applicants but only 45% of equally qualified female applicants. What DPDPA issue exists?', '["None, AI decisions are objective","Violates accuracy obligation (Section 8(3)) due to algorithmic bias creating unfair outcomes","Only an issue if explicitly programmed","Acceptable if disclosed to users"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, true, 'advanced'),
  ('What is LIME in the context of Explainable AI (XAI)?', '["Legal Information Management Engine","Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations","Limited Information Minimal Exposure","Layered Intelligence Model Engine"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('Under Section 8(3), why is accuracy particularly important for AI systems?', '["It''s not, AI is exempt from accuracy requirements","Biased training data violates accuracy obligation; inaccurate data leads to unfair AI decisions","Accuracy only matters for traditional databases","AI systems self-correct so accuracy isn''t a concern"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('What is a ''Model Extraction Attack''?', '["Physically stealing servers containing models","Querying a model repeatedly to reconstruct it and steal IP/data insights","Extracting features from raw data","Removing trained models from production"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('[SCENARIO] Your company uses ChatGPT (free version) and employees paste customer emails with personal data for summarization. What is the DPDPA issue?', '["No issue, ChatGPT is a tool like email","Unauthorized third-party data transfer without consent or DPA; personal data sent to OpenAI","Issue only if sensitive personal data is involved","OpenAI is a Data Fiduciary so no concern"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, true, 'advanced'),
  ('What is the purpose of an ''AI Model Card''?', '["Payment card for AI services","Standardized documentation of model''s purpose, training data, performance, and limitations","Business card for AI developers","Credit scoring card generated by AI"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('Under EU AI Act risk classification, which AI systems are prohibited (Unacceptable Risk)?', '["All AI systems in healthcare","Social scoring by governments, subliminal manipulation","Any AI using personal data","AI systems without human oversight"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('What does ''Differential Privacy'' add to data/models?', '["Encryption","Carefully calibrated noise to prevent identification of individuals","Access controls","Watermarks"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('If a Data Principal exercises right to erasure, what challenge does this pose for AI?', '["No challenge, just delete from database","Need to remove data''s influence from already-trained models (machine unlearning)","Can ignore since AI is exempt","Only affects future model training"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced'),
  ('[SCENARIO] A fintech uses AI to predict loan defaults. A customer requests erasure of their data. The company says AI models can''t be modified. Is this acceptable?', '["Yes, technical impossibility is a valid excuse","No, must implement machine unlearning OR retrain model OR cease using that model for the individual","Yes, if mentioned in privacy policy","Only acceptable for older models"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, true, 'advanced'),
  ('What is ''prompt engineering for privacy'' in the context of GenAI?', '["Making prompts longer to confuse AI","Designing prompts that don''t include personal data while still achieving the goal","Encrypting prompts before sending","Only using AI in private mode"]'::jsonb, 1, 6, false, 'advanced');
insert into public.risk_assessment (prompt, sort_order) values
  ('Discover - Do you have a complete, current inventory of every personal-data flow across cloud, on-premise, vendors, and AI tools?', 1),
  ('Define - Can you show a documented purpose, lawful basis, and retention period for each category of personal data you process?', 2),
  ('Design - Are your privacy notices, consent capture, and consent-withdrawal flows DPDP-ready and in clear, plain language?', 3),
  ('Defend - If a breach happened today, could you contain it and notify the Board and affected people within 72 hours?', 4),
  ('Deploy - Have DPDP processes, role-based training, and signed vendor DPAs actually rolled out across every department?', 5),
  ('Demonstrate - Could you hand an auditor or the Data Protection Board evidence of your compliance on demand?', 6),
  ('Drive - Does someone own DPDP day-to-day, with regular Data Principal rights, grievance, and AI-privacy reviews?', 7);
